[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Backend requirements
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirement

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Requirements for the FastAPI backend and web admin in ``backend/``. Verifications live in ``docs/verifications/backend/``.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Setup and authentication

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-010
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: First-run setup
STATEMENT: >>>
While no user with a login exists, the web admin shall offer a setup wizard that creates the first administrator. Once a login user exists, the setup pages shall redirect to the login page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A fresh installation ships without accounts or default passwords.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-011
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Web sessions
STATEMENT: >>>
Web admin pages shall require a logged-in session (cookie ``buddyplan_session``); administrator pages shall additionally require administrator rights.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-012
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: API tokens per device
STATEMENT: >>>
``POST /api/auth/login`` shall exchange a valid username and password plus a device ID for a bearer token. Logging in again from the same device shall replace that device's token. Tokens shall be stored only as a peppered hash.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-013
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Device revocation
STATEMENT: >>>
A user shall be able to list and revoke their own logged-in devices, and an administrator those of any user. Requests with a revoked token shall get HTTP 401.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-014
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Required secrets
STATEMENT: >>>
The backend shall refuse to start without ``SESSION_SECRET_KEY`` and ``TOKEN_PEPPER``, unless ``BUDDYPLAN_DEV=1`` is set.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Prevents running production with guessable or missing secrets.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: People and permissions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-020
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: User management
STATEMENT: >>>
An administrator shall be able to create, edit, reorder and delete people, and set per person whether they can log in and whether they are an administrator.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-021
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Agenda managers
STATEMENT: >>>
Each person shall have a list of people who may manage their agenda, by default the person themself. Only those people shall be able to create, edit or delete that person's agenda items.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-022
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Task managers
STATEMENT: >>>
The task system shall be enabled per person, with a list of people who may manage that person's tasks. Only those people shall be able to create, edit, move, reorder or delete that person's tasks. Completing tasks follows REQ-BE-024.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-023
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Own profile
STATEMENT: >>>
A logged-in user shall be able to change their own name, e-mail address, password and profile colour.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Who may complete tasks
STATEMENT: >>>
A task occurrence shall be marked as done only when requested by the person the task belongs to, by one of that person's task managers, by an administrator, or by a device logged in as a wall tablet. Other requests shall get HTTP 403 with a Dutch error message.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Children tick off their own tasks on their phone or on the shared wall tablet without needing rights to change them.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
'Logged in as a wall tablet' means the token was issued with device type 'dashboard' (REQ-BE-012). The device type is declared by the client at login.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-022

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Tasks

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-030
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Task contents
STATEMENT: >>>
A task shall have a title, an optional description, a person, a date and an icon.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-031
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Recurrence
STATEMENT: >>>
Tasks and agenda items shall support the repeat types once, daily, weekly, every two weeks and selected weekdays, with an optional end date. A repeating item shall not occur before its start date or after its end date.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-032
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Completion per occurrence
STATEMENT: >>>
Completing a repeating task shall mark only the occurrence on the given date as done.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-033
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Move and reorder
STATEMENT: >>>
Task managers shall be able to move a task to another date and to set the order of tasks within a day.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Agenda

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-040
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Manual agenda items
STATEMENT: >>>
Agenda managers shall be able to create, edit and delete agenda items with a title, date, optional start and end time and the repeat options of REQ-BE-031.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-041
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: iCal feeds
STATEMENT: >>>
A person shall be able to subscribe to iCal feeds (HTTPS or webcal URL) with a label, sync interval (15 minutes, 1 hour or 1 day), title prefix, colour and the choice to show times. The backend shall import the feeds in the background, honouring each feed's interval, including repeating events.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-042
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Google Calendar
STATEMENT: >>>
Once an administrator has configured OAuth credentials, a person shall be able to connect their Google account, choose which calendars to import and filter events by colour. The backend shall sync the chosen calendars about every 10 minutes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-043
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Imported items are read-only
STATEMENT: >>>
Agenda items imported from iCal or Google shall not be editable through Buddyplan (HTTP 403).
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Dashboard API

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dashboard change token
STATEMENT: >>>
``GET /api/dashboard/etag`` shall return a value that changes whenever data shown on the dashboard changes: creating, editing, reordering, moving, completing or deleting tasks, creating, editing or deleting agenda items, and changing a person's profile.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The wall tablet only reloads its data when this value changes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dashboard range limit
STATEMENT: >>>
``GET /api/dashboard`` shall accept date ranges of up to 12 weeks (83 days) and shall reject longer ranges with HTTP 400.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Wall tablet upgrades

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-050
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Display APK distribution
STATEMENT: >>>
An administrator shall be able to upload a new display app APK. The API shall report the uploaded version to the tablets and serve the APK for download to logged-in devices.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Afvalwijzer (optional)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-060
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Waste collection schedule
STATEMENT: >>>
When configured with a Dutch postcode and house number, the backend shall fetch the collection schedule from mijnafvalwijzer.nl.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-061
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Waste tasks
STATEMENT: >>>
Per waste type an administrator shall be able to choose who puts the bin out and who brings it back in, and when (the day before, the same day or the day after). The backend shall create these as normal tasks, on request and automatically every Sunday at 02:00 for the coming week.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: General

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-070
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Dutch interface
STATEMENT: >>>
All user-facing text, including API error messages, shall be in Dutch.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-071
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Automatic migrations
STATEMENT: >>>
On startup the backend shall bring the database schema up to date without losing existing data.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
